<header><p class="enc-kicker">Place · region</p><h1 class="enc-title">Azad Kashmir</h1><p class="enc-meta">Also known as Azad Jammu and Kashmir</p></header>
<div class="enc-body"><p class="enc-desc">Azad <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/kashmir">Kashmir</a> is a self-governing territory administered by <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/pakistan">Pakistan</a> in the western part of the former princely state of <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/jammu">Jammu</a> and Kashmir, with its capital at Muzaffarabad. It was formed in 1947 after a rising in Poonch and the First Kashmir War, and its boundary with Indian-administered Jammu and Kashmir follows the ceasefire line of 1949, later the Line of Control.</p><figure class="enc-fig"><img src="/images/encyclopedia/azad-kashmir.jpg" alt="Azad Kashmir" width="320" height="221" fetchpriority="high"><figcaption>Image: Ishtiaq Ali Khan · CC BY-SA 4.0 · <a href="https://commons.wikimedia.org/wiki/File:Neeulm_Valley_AJK_(Arang_Kel).jpg" target="_blank" rel="noopener">Wikimedia Commons</a></figcaption></figure></div>
